      "message": "Patch Set 1:\n\n(1 comment)\n\nAI code review results below, please doublecheck\n\nLooks good. The removal is complete and self-consistent: no references to SOCKNAL_BACKOFF, SOCKNAL_BACKOFF_MS, ENABLE_BACKOFF, ksnd_backoff_init/ksnd_backoff_max or the backoff/nobackoff deb profiles remain anywhere in the tree, and the only caller of ksocknal_lib_setup_sock() just propagates rc, so dropping the two early error returns changes nothing. One optional commit-message wording nit inline for whenever this is next refreshed - no need to re-spin for it.",
